WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
INTRO:
When the pandemic hit, companies either blew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:08.800
up or they got destroyed. Companies that benefited&nbsp;
from people staying at home like Zoom, Google,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:14.960
Amazon, and Facebook went to the moon. Meanwhile,&nbsp;
restaurants, airlines, cruise lines, and hotels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:20.640
went into the abyss, and many of them even filed&nbsp;
for bankruptcy. One of the biggest beneficiaries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.280
of the movement towards stay-at-home products&nbsp;
was an exercise equipment company called Peleton.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.240
Basically overnight, they became iconic for making&nbsp;
high-end exercise bikes and treadmills, and their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:36.800
stock boomed almost 10x from the pandemic lows.&nbsp;
But ever since the start of 2021, Peloton has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.840
been doing so well. They’ve had to recall a couple&nbsp;
of products, face a few PR nightmares, slash the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.000
prices of their products by hundreds of dollars,&nbsp;
watch their products oversaturate 2nd hand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.440
markets, lose their CEO, and burn more&nbsp;
money than ever before. As you would guess,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.480
the stock market hasn’t been very kind to this&nbsp;
lackluster performance, and the stock has sold off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:02.640
86% from the peak. So, here’s the rise and fall of&nbsp;
one of the biggest fads in the fitness industry.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.520
BOUGIE BIKING:&nbsp;

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:13.200
Taking a look back, the story of Peloton circles&nbsp;
back to a man named John Foley. We don’t know too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:17.440
much about John’s background other than the fact&nbsp;
that he seems like a traditional businessman who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.920
climbed the corporate ladder. He got prestigious&nbsp;
degrees in engineering and business from Georgia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.240
Tech and Harvard respectively. And through&nbsp;
decades of work, he was able to become the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:31.200
president of e-commerce at Barnes &amp; Noble. At&nbsp;
this point, most people would probably just try&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:35.600
to work up to the C suite, work for another&nbsp;
10 20 years and then retire comfortably.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:41.280
But, it looks like John had an entrepreneurial&nbsp;
urge that he had never tended to. So, in 2012,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.880
at age 40, John made the fateful decision to quit&nbsp;
his job and give business a shot. He didn’t want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:51.120
to do it alone though, so he convinced a bunch of&nbsp;
his executive friends to take the plunge with him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:56.560
This included Graham Stanton, Hisao Kushi, Tom&nbsp;
Cortese, and Yony Feng. And given all of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:02.080
connections and personal wealth itself, it wasn’t&nbsp;
difficult to raise money. Just one month after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:06.960
starting the company, they were able to raise&nbsp;
$400,000, and by the end of their first year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:12.480
they were able to raise another $3.5 million.&nbsp;
Since then, Peloton has managed to raise over $1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.200
billion from the private markets. But anyway,&nbsp;
with their first few millions, they started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.160
developing their flagship product which is their&nbsp;
exercise bike. The idea was to allow people to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:27.280
enjoy a high-end cycling class from the comfort of&nbsp;
their homes. Each bike comes with a massive screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:31.920
that’s capable of live streaming workouts from&nbsp;
dozens of their personal trainers. The product&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.960
wasn’t anything game-changing per se, but it&nbsp;
provided a unique twist to a classic product,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:42.800
and usually, that’s all you need. People often&nbsp;
get stuck up with trying to find the next big idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:48.400
when the best idea is actually just to noticeably&nbsp;
improve something that already exists. Anyway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.560
Peloton turned to Kickstarter to launch their&nbsp;
first bike with a goal of raising $250,000.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:58.480
They were only able to garner a total of 297&nbsp;
backers, but given that each bike cost over a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:04.320
$1000, they were able to beat their goal and&nbsp;
raise $307,000. Peloton would turn around and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:09.040
release their bikes to the general public in&nbsp;
2014, and with that Peloton was in business.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:13.120
RISE TO GLORY:&nbsp;

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.680
Over the next few years, Peloton slowly&nbsp;
grew a core base of hardcore users.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:22.240
Initially, their products mainly appealed to real&nbsp;
biking enthusiasts who wanted a solid alternative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:27.120
to biking outside or attending a real cycling&nbsp;
class. But with time, their demographic would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:32.720
shift closer and closer to everyday people. In&nbsp;
May of 2018, Peloton would attempt to expand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:37.760
their audience by targeting enthusiast runners as&nbsp;
well with the launch of the peloton Tread+. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:43.920
the Tread+ carried an even more bougie price than&nbsp;
their bikes starting at $4300. It should also be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:48.480
noted that if you want access to all of Peloton’s&nbsp;
classes and live streams, you have to get their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:54.880
All-Access subscription which costs $39 per&nbsp;
month or $468 per year itself. For those prices,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:59.440
I’m pretty sure it would be way cheaper to get a&nbsp;
gym membership and just attend cycling classes in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:05.360
person. If a gym membership costs $30 per month,&nbsp;
it would take nearly 12 years to pay the $4300&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:10.960
that it would cost to just get the Tread+. Despite&nbsp;
these crazy prices, for people who highly valued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:15.920
the live-streamed classes and the convenience,&nbsp;
there was no better at-home alternative. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.320
with time, their high price tags started to&nbsp;
become more of an advantage than a hindrance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:25.200
Similar to other high-end brands like Apple and&nbsp;
Louis Vuitton, Peloton’s high prices gave them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:30.000
exclusivity and turned their products into status&nbsp;
symbols. If you were able to spend thousands on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.600
an exercise bike and hundreds on a subscription&nbsp;
every year, you clearly had money. In my opinion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:39.760
if you don’t know what Peloton means, you&nbsp;
probably shouldn’t be getting their bikes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:45.680
and this is how it mostly was till 2020. But, once&nbsp;
the pandemic hit, a large portion of white-collar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:50.320
workers decided that it was a great idea to buy&nbsp;
some high-end equipment to start exercising on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:55.200
And over the next few quarters, Peloton’s revenue&nbsp;
numbers would hit new all-time highs and they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.200 --> 00:05:00.080
would even post a few profitable quarters. But,&nbsp;
while Peloton was doing better than ever before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:04.000
financially, they were concurrently dealing&nbsp;
with a slew of problems in the background.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:08.080
ROCKY ROAD:&nbsp;

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:12.720
One aspect that most YouTubers are extremely&nbsp;
careful of is avoiding copyrighted music.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:18.000
Even just a couple of seconds of copyrighted&nbsp;
music can get an entire video demonetized.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.560
Unfortunately, it looks like Peloton didn’t&nbsp;
have any YouTubers on their design team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:27.520
because they filled their workout videos&nbsp;
with copyrighted music. And in March of 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:32.160
the National Music Publishers Association&nbsp;
would hit Peloton with a $150 million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:36.960
lawsuit. Peloton instantly responded by removing&nbsp;
the copyrighted music from all of their courses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:42.400
and even removing certain courses that depended on&nbsp;
the music. Most of Peloton’s users weren’t exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:46.720
happy with this change given that copyrighted&nbsp;
music is generally better than noncopyrighted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:53.120
music. But Peloton’s customers weren’t the only&nbsp;
ones that were unhappy. In September of 2019, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:57.440
music association would double their allegations&nbsp;
on Peloton claiming a total of $300 million.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.560
Peloton did end up settling for an undisclosed&nbsp;
amount that was likely lower than $300 million,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:08.880
but I doubt this was a very good experience for&nbsp;
Peloton. Shortly after, they would find themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:13.360
in yet another controversy with a commercial&nbsp;
called “The Gift That Gives Back.” The plot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:17.840
of the commercial is a husband buying his wife a&nbsp;
Peleton bike and the wife becoming a lot more fit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:23.200
and athletic over the next year. Most people would&nbsp;
just dismiss the commercial as another fitness ad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:28.320
and not think much about it. But, a select group&nbsp;
of people felt that Peloton was promoting body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:32.400
shaming and that the plot of the commercial&nbsp;
implied that the husband was dissatisfied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:37.520
with the wife’s physical appearance. Honestly,&nbsp;
it’s just a traditional fitness commercial,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:42.400
but the like to dislike ratio shows how divided&nbsp;
people were on the advertisement. Despite all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:47.040
these controversies, Peloton sales continued to&nbsp;
rise through the start of the pandemic, but this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:52.240
led to its own issues. Peloton couldn’t keep up&nbsp;
with the massive influx of new orders, and many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:57.120
customers had waiting times that stretched several&nbsp;
months. This led to many customers reconsidering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:01.520
their orders and canceling them a few months&nbsp;
into the wait. While these growing pains were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:06.240
likely annoying to deal with, it soon became clear&nbsp;
that Peloton had much more deep-rooted problems.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:12.400
THE LONGEVITY PROBLEM:
The truth is that a significant portion of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:17.840
people who went ahead and bought a Peloton didn’t&nbsp;
actually stick to using the Peloton. The thing is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:22.960
most of these guys weren’t enthusiast bikers or&nbsp;
runners. They were actually the type of people who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:27.200
got a gym membership as a new year’s resolution&nbsp;
and then only used it 5 times throughout the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:32.960
entire year. And, buying a Peloton was basically&nbsp;
their Covid resolution. Many of them likely felt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:37.120
that by spending a significant amount of money and&nbsp;
having live training classes, they would be more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:42.160
compelled to work out. And while this may have&nbsp;
worked for a few months or even several months,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:45.920
as people began to return to their normal&nbsp;
lives, their fitness lives also returned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:50.560
to being nonexistent. Most of these guys kept&nbsp;
their Pelotons around for a few more months,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:54.960
but eventually, they decided to sell them on&nbsp;
eBay and Craigslist leading to these sites&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:59.360
being flooded with Peloton listings. Not only did&nbsp;
these listings attract buying traffic away from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:04.160
Peloton’s official website, but it sent a pretty&nbsp;
strong signal that everyday people who bought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:09.600
a Peloton didn’t really find it that valuable.&nbsp;
This isn’t to say that Peloton doesn’t make great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:14.400
products because their bikes and treadmills&nbsp;
are truly top of the line. These buyers were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:19.440
simply not part of the target demographic, and as&nbsp;
they left the scene, Peloton’s revenue started to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:25.040
stagnate and decline. As Peloton started to fall&nbsp;
out of favor amongst everyday consumers, people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:30.000
and companies started to poke fun at Peloton. Ryan&nbsp;
Reynold’s, for example, hired the actress that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.640
played the wife in the Peloton commercial to star&nbsp;
in a gin commercial called “The Gift That Doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:40.160
Give Back”. Similarly, just a few months ago, HBO&nbsp;
aired an episode in which a character called Mr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:44.720
Big suffers from a heart attack and dies after&nbsp;
riding a Peloton. Peloton shares would fall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:50.480
11.3% the day after this episode aired on TV.&nbsp;
Clearly, Peloton was suffering from a fleeting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:56.000
customer base and shifting public image, but it&nbsp;
didn’t long for things to go from bad to worse.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:00.000
THE COLLAPSE:&nbsp;

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.520
The nail in the coffin for Peloton came in March&nbsp;
of 2021 when a video was released of a child being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:10.480
sucked into the back of a Peloton treadmill&nbsp;
and dying. Following this story, we saw dozens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:14.880
of reports suggesting that adults, children,&nbsp;
and pets were injured due to Peloton products.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:20.320
Honestly, I’m not sure why Peloton received so&nbsp;
much heat when a lot of the fault is shared by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:24.880
the users of their products. Nevertheless,&nbsp;
Peloton implemented a slew of software-based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:29.200
safety features within the next month. But,&nbsp;
this wasn’t enough to appease all the criticism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:34.560
they were receiving from the media. And in&nbsp;
May of 2021, Peloton would finally give in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:39.920
and issue a recall for their Tread and Tread+&nbsp;
treadmills which is valid till November of 2022.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:44.720
And Peloton has been losing hundreds of millions&nbsp;
per quarter ever since. Honestly, I suspect that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:49.120
a lot of the returns are just people cashing&nbsp;
in on an impulse purchase as opposed to people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:53.200
returning these treadmills due to legitimate&nbsp;
safety concerns. I guess it was just these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:58.400
customers’ lucky day. Given all this negative&nbsp;
PR and the oversaturated second-hand market,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:02.880
Peloton was forced to slash prices to continue&nbsp;
appealing to customers which has just made it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:08.320
even harder to turn a profit. As losses continue&nbsp;
to pile up, Peloton has been forced to make harder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:13.040
and harder decisions. One of these decisions&nbsp;
came in early February when Peloton went ahead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:17.920
and reduced their workforce by 2800 employees.&nbsp;
This was around the same time that John Foley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:23.440
resigned from the company and was replaced by&nbsp;
Barry McCarthy. So far, John lost his position&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:31.840
as CEO and his status as a billionaire. The only&nbsp;
question left is, will John also lose his company?

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:34.000
UNCERTAIN FUTURE:&nbsp;

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:39.520
Looking forward, while Peloton is definitely in a&nbsp;
terrible position right now, I think it’s unlikely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:44.400
that they’ll file for bankruptcy and completely&nbsp;
shut down. Despite all their ups and downs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:49.440
Peloton has been able to grow a strong base of&nbsp;
core users that wouldn’t use anything else. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:53.840
just maintaining this customer base could be quite&nbsp;
lucrative for Peloton given the high subscription&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:59.440
fees. With that being said though, the next few&nbsp;
quarters don’t look that great as it’s unlikely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:04.640
that Peloton can really start to build up positive&nbsp;
momentum again until the recall period is over.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:08.960
Even after the recall is over, it’s unlikely&nbsp;
that Peloton will ever enjoy the same amount&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:14.000
of interest and excitement that they enjoyed at&nbsp;
the peak of the pandemic. But, over several years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:17.840
it’s possible that they’re able to build up a&nbsp;
large enough base of enthusiasts that they’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:23.280
able to pull in more revenue and profit than&nbsp;
ever before, but we’ll just have to wait and see.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:27.760
Do you think Peloton will rise from the ashes or&nbsp;
do you think it will become an infamous fitness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:33.120
fad? Comment that down below. Also, drop a&nbsp;
like if you think Peloton’s are overpriced.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:36.480
And of course, consider checking out our&nbsp;
international channels to watch our videos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:40.400
in other languages and consider subscribing&nbsp;
to see more questions logically answered.

